<h1>Triggers</h1>

<p>Database triggers allow you to run in-database stored procedures in response to DML queries.</p>

<p>SQL Relay extends this paradigm by allowing you to run in-database or os-level tasks in response to any query.</p>

<p><img src="../images/triggers.png"/></p>

<p>The standard SQL Relay distribution includes several trigger modules, including:</p>

<ul>
  <li><b>replay</b> - provides automatic deadlock resolution via transaction replay</li>
  <li><b>savepoints</b> - contains failed queries to a savepoint so they don't abort the surrounding transaction</li>
  <li><b>upsert</b> - automatically converts inserts to updates when the insert fails</li>
</ul>

<p>Custom trigger modules can be developed too.</p>

